#547 spot channels 1c-2a: flat and layered TIFF fixtures with spot channels, authored by Adobe
Photoshop 2025 26.10.0 (scripts/photoshop-probe/spot_tiff_take.py, take2, run
20261026T230703Z-a8b8762a; receipts in ~/devel/doctored-fixtures/photoshop/spot-tiff-547/take2.
take1 was skipped before anything was driven: a Photoshop the run had not launched was open).

Each file starts from one of the runner's PNG scenes: S, 32 x 8 opaque, gray v(x) =
round(255 x / 31); St, the same with alpha 0 at x >= 28. The spot channels are 1b's
(spot_psd_take.py): one Make of a new spot channel each, filled from the selection:

  Spot Ramp     Lab (55, 70, 30), from the Red channel loaded as the selection: coverage v(x)
  Spot Bloc é   Lab (80, -20, 60), from the rectangle x in [8, 24), y in [2, 6): full inside

  file          mode, depth   scene   kind      spots (solidity %)
  rgb8.tif      RGB 8         S       flat      Ramp 0, Bloc 100
  rgb8_t.tif    RGB 8         St      flat      Bloc 50 (with a transparency)
  rgb16.tif     RGB 16        S       flat      Ramp 50, Bloc 100
  cmyk8.tif     CMYK 8        S       flat      Ramp 100, Bloc 0
  cmyk16.tif    CMYK 16       S       flat      Ramp 50
  rgb8_l.tif    RGB 8         St      layered   Ramp 0, Bloc 100
  cmyk16_l.tif  CMYK 16       St      layered   Ramp 50

Saved as copies with TiffSaveOptions (alpha channels, spot colors and transparency on; layers
per kind; no compression; byte order MACOS; profile embedded), reopened by Photoshop with every
spot's name, kind SPOTCOLOR, solidity and Lab as declared. The two PDFs of the take (rgb8.pdf,
cmyk16.pdf) are not committed: both keep the spots as /Separation colourants (PDF-FORM
SEPARATIONS).

photoshop.json holds, for each file, its sha256, bytes, mode, depth, kind, the directory's
layout (byte order, Photometric, SamplesPerPixel, BitsPerSample, ExtraSamples, Planar,
Compression, tag 34377's resource ids and the channel resources as hex, the first saved sample),
the PLACE, POLARITY and COMPOSITE readings, and per spot its name, declared and readback Lab,
solidity, DisplayInfo kind and colour space, the stored Lab words and the stored rows.

What the flat files say, which is the reader's and writer's spec (core/src/tiff_spot_samples.rs,
core/src/tiff_spot.rs): one MM directory, uncompressed chunky strips; a spot channel is a
TRAILING extra sample after the colour samples and the transparency, ExtraSamples 0 (the
transparency is ExtraSamples 1); its samples are stored INVERTED, max - coverage, in RGB and
CMYK alike (H1); the composite holds no overprint (C0); tag 34377 holds the PSD's 1006 (Mac
Roman), 1045, 1077 (kind 2, Lab) and 1053 (ids from 3) and no 1007, every list leading with
"Transparency" (kind 1, id 0) when the file has one (L1). The layered files carry the same
trailing extras on their composite and tag 37724 (Layr / Lr16); they are recorded for 1c-2b.

Read by core/tests/spot_tiff_photoshop.rs, which SKIPs when this folder is absent.
